t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The Trump Administration sees no indication of a coordinated cyberattack, state-sponsored activity, or malign actor behind the recent tech outages.</strong> Director of National Intelligence Jay Clayton and National Security Adviser Marco Rubio made clear that these are separate incidents caused by companies patching vulnerabilities and upgrading outdated systems, with America leading the effort to harden its digital infrastructure.</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>DNI Clayton:</strong> “This is not a cyberattack, and this is not a coordinated effort by a nation state. We’ve looked very closely. Anytime we see something like this, those are the first questions that we ask on behalf of the American people, and we go across and we say, ‘Is that what’s going on here?’ <strong>That is not what’s going on here.</strong>” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2122799793218969745\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Secretary Rubio:</strong> “We have no indication, no evidence, and no reason to believe at all that any of these incidents are related to each other. In essence, <strong>the Microsoft incident has nothing to do with what we saw with the FAA. The FAA has nothing to do with what we saw with the banks a few days ago</strong>… We have zero evidence or any reason to believe that any of these isolated or individual instances have anything to do with nefarious actors, with cyber hackers, with criminals, with another nation-state, with a malign actor of any kind.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2122861266146587028\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>DNI Clayton:</strong> “We do not see the indicia of a coordinated cyberattack — let me just be clear about that — and we do not see the indicia of state-sponsored activity here. And we can be fairly confident in that because we know those things exist, and we’ve been looking for them in the past.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2122800369075994738\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Secretary Rubio:</strong> “People are fearful, people are uncertain — and the best way to deal with people’s uncertainty and discomfort is to share with them transparently what we know and what we believe in terms of the information we have before us… <strong>We are not under systemic attack</strong>… Every indicator we have is that every single one of these events has an explanation or a cause that has nothing to do with a cyber-criminal, has nothing to do with a hostile actor or another country… <strong>The American people should have confidence in that.</strong>” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2122863623504556066\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>DNI Clayton:</strong> “Let me tell you what we think this is, and we think that it is with confidence. Lots of institutions, because these vulnerabilities have been identified, are patching. They’re taking their systems down, they’re upgrading them, they’re putting patches in place… This is being done on much larger scale because everybody, and it’s a good news story, everybody recognizes it’s time to upgrade their systems. <strong>And as they upgrade them, they’re not coming back as expected in all cases. And in some cases, systems have to hand off to other systems, and those handoffs are not coming back as expected.</strong> But this is just an upgrade in patching, an upgrade in systems.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2122800369075994738\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Secretary Rubio:</strong> “Sometimes when you are going in to fix your system because you’ve identified a vulnerability, it creates a short-term disruption in the way your system works… <strong>Companies, which is a good thing, are now immediately sharing vulnerabilities because they don’t want to be accused of covering up something.</strong>” (<a href=\"https://www.mediaite.com/media/news/marco-rubio-holds-presser-to-try-and-reassure-the-public-amid-outages/\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>DNI Clayton:</strong> “As a result of SI and the ability to scan systems more quickly, the ability to identify vulnerabilities has increased. That is why it is so incumbent upon all of us to work together to patch, to report vulnerabilities, and <strong>it is where the U.S. is leading.</strong>” (<a href=\"https://www.foxbusiness.com/video/6408513620112\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>DNI Clayton:</strong> “<strong>Our systems need upgrades. They need patching.</strong> We have legacy systems, and they’re more and more interconnected, and they’re handling more and more traffic… Thankfully, the U.S. is leading and is far ahead in that step change in technology… <strong>We’re going to come out the other side much better.</strong>” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2122878235125879293\">Watch</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/11/no-indication-of-a-cyberattack-dni-clayton-and-secretary-rubio-on-recent-tech-outages/\">“No Indication of a Cyberattack”: DNI Clayton and Secretary Rubio on Recent Tech Outages</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
